+---
+id: dl-004-importtasks-reports-bad-lines-in-its-result-and-never-throws
+type: decision-log
+title: "importTasks reports bad lines in its result and never throws"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+
+## Context
+
+Teams import spreadsheet rows; some rows will be wrong. The domain must not throw (r4).
+
+## Decision
+
+`importTasks` returns `{ imported, rejected }` instead of a `Result`: a bad line never stops the others.
+Each line goes through `list.add`, so it gets the same validation (decision dl-003) and duplicate check;
+the reason is that error's message. A line with more than three `;` fields is rejected rather than
+guessed at. Priorities are matched exactly (no case folding), after trimming. Line numbers count every
+line, blank ones included, and `\n`, `\r\n` and `\r` all end a line. A title repeated in the text is
+rejected as a duplicate. Not atomic: valid lines stay added even if others are rejected.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Callers show `rejected` to the user and need no try/catch.
+- Spreadsheet titles containing `;` cannot be imported.
